[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Create the dependency policy and public contracts that keep the deterministic
[stderr] shared core independent of browser, renderer, clock, network, and platform
[stderr] modules. Adapters may submit commands and render returned state/events only.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0001 is an implementation dependency. Author and validate this contract now;
[stderr] do not treat GATE-0001 as permission to implement or as a blocker to authoring.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `src/core/public interfaces` and the `Command`, state, event, and adapter interfaces.
[stderr] - `src/platform/{web,pwa}/adapter interfaces` and the dependency-policy manifest.
[stderr] - `architecture dependency rules` and `docs/architecture.md`.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Define an enforceable import direction in which the core accepts shared
[stderr] commands, validates and returns state/events, while web and PWA adapters
[stderr] translate platform input and render those returned values. The adapter must not
[stderr] mutate campaign state directly. Keep the policy framework-neutral so a later
[stderr] tool decision can choose its enforcement mechanism without changing the seam.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] Both targets consume the same core contract. The web adapter owns browser
[stderr] input, rendering, and viewport integration; the PWA adapter additionally owns
[stderr] installation and cache-lifecycle adaptation. Neither target imports platform
[stderr] concerns into the core or becomes a campaign authority.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Non-goals
[stderr] 
[stderr] Do not implement combat, exploration, screens, campaign rules, accounts,
[stderr] network clients, renderer behaviour, or target-specific rules. Do not create
[stderr] assets, artwork, fonts, icons, audio, maps, or copied reference styling.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Asset assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. This interface and dependency-policy work
[stderr] must not create incidental product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Verification
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Add a dependency-rule test that rejects forbidden core imports.
[stderr] - Add a fixture adapter proving command-only interaction and returned
[stderr]   state/event rendering.
[stderr] - Record the selected enforcement mechanism only after the retained GATE-0001
[stderr]   tool decision; do not claim that gate is resolved here.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Evidence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Preserve the dependency-rule test result, the fixture-adapter result, and an
[stderr] architecture document showing the one-way core/adapter boundary.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Forbidden imports into the core are rejected.
[stderr] - A fixture adapter can submit commands and consume returned state/events
[stderr]   without directly mutating campaign state.
[stderr] - The shared contract remains usable by web and PWA adapters without choosing
[stderr]   implementation tooling or creating product assets.
