[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Generate only the bootstrap wave of ordinary Supervisor runbooks in
[stderr] `projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks/`: a bounded catalogue-expansion
[stderr] task followed by a dispatcher task. The dispatcher allocates at most ten
[stderr] authoring B-series tasks per wave, creates one successor dispatcher, and stops.
[stderr] Each authoring task instructs Codex to create only its assigned R-series
[stderr] implementation runbooks under
[stderr] `projects/<project-slug>/runbooks/`, then validate their metadata and update the
[stderr] manifest. The successor dispatcher repeats this process until no queued
[stderr] catalogue chapter or unassigned implementation contract remains. Generate an
[stderr] `INITIAL.md` context document in `authoring-runbooks/`
[stderr] that points to the canonical `PROJECT_BRIEF.md` and specification.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Register the generated authoring collection with the source collection by
[stderr] writing `runbooks/.supervisor-children/<project-slug>.json` containing
[stderr] `{"runbooks_dir": "../projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks"}`. Also
[stderr] write `authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json` containing
[stderr] `{"runbooks_dir": "../runbooks"}`. These are explicit child-collection
[stderr] registrations; `supervisor-run --run-all` follows them automatically after the
[stderr] parent collection is accepted.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every dispatcher first expands at most one queued specification/catalogue domain
[stderr] chapter (maximum 250 `IMP-*` contracts), validates its coverage, then allocates
[stderr] ready contracts. If any queued chapter or ready contract remains, it creates no
[stderr] more than ten authoring tasks and exactly one successor dispatcher. If none
[stderr] remains, it creates the final audit task instead. This is a durable loop, not a
[stderr] recursive prompt or an unbounded single run.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every generated R-series runbook must use the standard Supervisor front matter
[stderr] and contain: precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs; owned
[stderr] files/data/interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; platform differences;
[stderr] verification commands/evidence; and observable acceptance criteria. It must be
[stderr] small enough for one implementation task, not a vague epic.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every generated R-series runbook must retain machine-readable provenance to the
[stderr] canonical decisions that justify it. Its front matter must declare all of these
[stderr] non-empty fields, using comma-separated values where more than one applies:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```yaml
[stderr] source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#save-state
[stderr] source_catalogue_ids: IMP-SAVE-001
[stderr] authoring_batch: B0007
[stderr] factory_stages: F003,F005,F012,F013
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] `source_specifications` points to the smallest relevant canonical
[stderr] specification section; `source_catalogue_ids` identifies the allocated
[stderr] implementation-catalogue records; `authoring_batch` identifies the B-series
[stderr] writer that created the R file; and `factory_stages` identifies the F-series
[stderr] stages that established the requirement. This is a traceability trail, not an
[stderr] instruction to inject every F or B runbook into the implementation agent's
[stderr] prompt. The R task uses these links to read only the canonical context it needs.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every generated R-series runbook must also include a detailed asset assessment.
[stderr] Its front matter must always declare both fields below, even when no assets are
[stderr] needed:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```yaml
[stderr] asset_impact: required # or not_applicable
[stderr] asset_ids: village_gate_main,village_gate_construction # blank only when not_applicable
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] For `asset_impact: required`, the B-series writer must reserve stable,
[stderr] product-specific asset IDs (never generic names such as `image1`), provide an
[stderr] `asset_brief` and `visual_style_version`, and include an `## Asset assessment`
[stderr] section explaining the assets' purpose, where they appear, the required visual
[stderr] states/variants, source-of-truth ownership, and original-art acceptance checks.
[stderr] For `not_applicable`, that section must explain why the scope needs no generated
[stderr] or source visual asset and explicitly prohibit incidental asset creation. This
[stderr] keeps UI, illustration, icon, texture, sprite, audio-visual, and other product
[stderr] asset work visible in the implementation plan instead of discovering it midway
[stderr] through coding.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every generated R-series runbook must also declare an audio assessment, even
[stderr] when audio is not needed:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```yaml
[stderr] audio_impact: required # or not_applicable
[stderr] audio_ids: ember_menu_loop # blank only when not_applicable
[stderr] audio_brief: 30-second seamless instrumental menu cue # blank only when not_applicable
[stderr] audio_duration_seconds: 30 # 0 only when not_applicable
[stderr] audio_loop: required # required, not_required, or not_applicable
[stderr] audio_style_version: project-audio-v1
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] For `audio_impact: required`, the writer must reserve stable cue IDs, cite the
[stderr] relevant `04-audio-direction.md` section, describe the in-product trigger and
[stderr] mix/accessibility expectations, and assign a sensible duration and loop policy.
[stderr] The Supervisor's separate local audio lane then creates a manifest, invokes
[stderr] ACE-Step, and performs technical/provenance QA before coding begins. For
[stderr] `not_applicable`, every audio field has the stated empty/default form so an
[stderr] otherwise unrelated task cannot silently generate music or sound effects.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Each B-series authoring task may create at most seven R-series implementation
[stderr] runbooks. It must stop after its assigned seven (or fewer), update the manifest,
[stderr] and leave remaining work for the next bounded batch.
[stderr] 
[stderr] An unresolved framework, legal, service, design, or other human gate is never
[stderr] permission for a B-series writer to omit its assigned R files or wait for an
